{sov: Notes}
Modal Jazz Benchmark: The opening track of 1959's 'Kind of Blue', establishing
modal jazz frameworks based on entire scale modes rather than complex chord changes.

Form: 32-bar AABA structure (16 bars Dm7, 8 bars Ebm7, 8 bars Dm7).

"So What" Chords: Bill Evans' famous "So What" chord voicings consist of three
fourth intervals topped by a major third.
- For Dm7: Em7 (x7778x) resolving down to Dm7 (x5556x) or Em11 to Dm11.
- For Ebm7: Shift the exact same visual shape up one half-step (Fm7 to Ebm7).

Call and Response Theme: Paul Chambers' upright bass plays the lead "call" line,
answered by the sharp two-chord piano/horn stab on the "So What" response.

Improvisation: D Dorian over the A sections; Eb Dorian over the B section.
{eov}